  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="commodity_pentice_cloth_cb1116a7d6861cbebeb4ac9b7c09ff19010c06b84e308df797c7641d5b13333dcae">
    <crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>a painted or stained cloth: a decorative hanging for a room, painted or worked with figures, mottoes or texts (OED s.v. painted 5; cloth, painted); also an awning (pentice / penthouse cloth; Carlin 246). Attested as Latin pannus depictus (panno depicto, pannis depictis, pannorum depictorum, etc.), French drapz depictus, and English paynted/payntid cloth(es) and cloth(es) pictorum (painters' cloth).</crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>
    <crm:P2_has_type rdf:resource="http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object"/>
  </rdf:Description>
